From 9e21b3915bea7c10e50ca488ff9cfb8d2d4c9816 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: scada <scada@noreply.codeberg.org>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 07:32:19 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 65/78] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998: match the CPU capacities to
 the vendor energy model

The scheduler derived a little-core capacity of 528 from dmips 1024/1536,
while the vendor kernel's energy model (and the A53/A73 IPC gap) puts a
1.9 GHz Kryo 280 silver core at 419 of a 2.46 GHz gold core's 1024.
Overrating the little cores kept heavy single-threaded work on them too
long. Use 542/1024, which yields 419.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0144VMKxYe33NKa3LLPZNivr
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi | 16 ++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

